                <div style="font-size:12px; color:#e2e8f0; line-height:1.6;">
                    ✅ <strong>School Master:</strong> 600 / 600 unique schools<br/>
                    ✅ <strong>Attendance Records:</strong> 100% IDs matched (20,000 / 20,000)<br/>
                    ✅ <strong>Test Scores:</strong> 100% IDs matched (8,000 / 8,000)<br/>
                    ✅ <strong>MDM Procurement:</strong> 100% IDs matched (12,000 / 12,000)<br/>
                    ✅ <strong>Infrastructure:</strong> 100% IDs matched (3,000 / 3,000; 598 unique schools inspected)<br/>
                    ✅ <strong>Unmapped School IDs:</strong> 0 unmapped across all datasets
                </div>
            </div>
            """,
            unsafe_allow_html=True
        )

    st.markdown("<br/>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # Data Quality Flags & Limitations
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div style="background: rgba(30, 27, 75, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.3); padding: 18px; border-radius: 14px;">
            <div style="font-size:13px; font-weight:800; color:#c084fc; text-transform:uppercase; margin-bottom:6px;">📌 Analytical Boundaries & Methodological Limitations</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px; color:#cbd5e1; line-height:1.6;">
                • <strong>No Direct Student Dropout Label:</strong> The supplied datasets do not contain explicit dropout event labels. The <i>Retention Risk Indicator</i> is an analytical prioritization index.<br/>
                • <strong>Association vs. Causation:</strong> Observational statistical comparisons (e.g. electricity vs. test scores) describe association only and do not establish direct causation.<br/>
                • <strong>Preservation of Source Gaps:</strong> Missing values are retained or explicitly flagged as "Missing / Not Reported" rather than artificially imputed.<br/>
                • <strong>Scenario Projections:</strong> Policy simulator outputs represent hypothetical scenarios under linear assumptions rather than causal forecasts.
            </div>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

